{title: Be Strong and Courageous}
{subtitle: Joshua 1:1–9; Numbers 14:6–30; Joshua 3:14–17; 6:2–20; 24:14–24}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] |
| [Gm7] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Moses the servant of the Lord is dead
[Gm7]Now get up and cross this Jordan
[Eb]Every place where the sole of your foot treads
[Bb]I have given you just as promised
From the wilderness to the great sea
[Gm7]All this shall be your territory
[Eb]No one will be able to stand against you
As [F7sus4]I was with Moses so I will be with you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Be strong and courageous
[Gm7]For you will give this people possession
[Eb]Do not be terrified or [F]dismayed
[Eb]The Lord your [F]God is with [Bb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Joshua and Caleb tore their clothes
[Gm7]Saying the land is exceedingly good
[Eb]If the Lord delights in us
He will bring us into this land
[Bb]Flowing with milk and honey
Their protection is gone and the [F]Lord is with us
Do not fear [Bb]them
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be strong and courageous
[Gm7]For you will give this people possession
[Eb]Do not be terrified [F]or dismayed
[Eb]The Lord your [F]God is with [Bb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The Jordan was overflowing its banks
[Gm7]As it does all through the harvest season
The [Eb]feet of the priests touched the water's edge
[Bb]The water standing in a single heap
So the people crossed over opposite Jericho
[Gm7]The priests stood firm on dry ground
[Eb]In the middle of the Jordan
All Is[F]rael crossed on dry ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Be strong and courageous
[Gm7]For you will give this people possession
[Eb]Do not be terri[F]fied or dismayed
[Eb]The Lord [F]your God is with [Bb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
March around the city with all [Gm]your soldiers
Circling it [Eb]once for six days
Seven priests carry seven ram's-horn [Bb]trumpets
On the seventh day march seven times
The walls will fall at the sound of [Gm]the trumpets
As for me and my [Eb]house
We will [F]serve the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Be strong and [Gm]courageous
Do not be terrified or [Eb]dismayed
The Lord [F]your God is with [Bb]you
Wherever you go
{end_of_verse}
